     ppkkgg__cchheecckk — check consistency of installed packages

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ppkkgg__cchheecckk [--FFffIIiimmnnqqvvxx] [--DD _n_a_m_e[=_v_a_l_u_e]]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     ppkkgg__cchheecckk verifies as much information as it can about installed pack‐
     ages.

     ppkkgg__cchheecckk is not needed under normal circumstances, but it can be used to
     recover after a catastrophic system failure in the middle of a pkg_add(1)
     or pkg_delete(1).

     ppkkgg__cchheecckk performs the following checks:

     Packing-list sanity
            Checks that _/_v_a_r_/_d_b_/_p_k_g only contains directories, that each di‐
            rectory holds a packing-list, and that said packing-list is an ac‐
            tual packing-list that matches the directory.

     Direct dependencies
            Checks that all direct dependencies are recorded correctly,
            specifically, that @@ddeeppeenndd, @@ttaagg and @@wwaannttlliibb match actual pack‐
            ages.  It currently does not verify that @@wwaannttlliibb or @@ttaagg are
            reachable from the base package.

     Reverse dependencies
            Checks that all direct dependencies have corresponding reverse de‐
            pendencies.

     Files from packages
            Checks that each file, link or directory in those packing-lists
            actually exist, and that their checksum matches what's recorded in
            the packing-list.

     Other files (option --FF)
            Checks that there are no other random objects under _/_u_s_r_/_l_o_c_a_l.

     By default, ppkkgg__cchheecckk will only perform very safe transformations, such
     as the removal of core-dumps.  ppkkgg__cchheecckk will ask the user for more per‐
     manent changes in interactive mode, or perform them anyway with option
     --ff.

     The options are as follows:

     --DD _n_a_m_e[=_v_a_l_u_e]
             Extra options.  Recognized keywords include:

             nnoossiigg     Do not check digital signatures.

     --FF      Check the filesystem for random objects.

     --ff      Force the removal of bogus package information.

     --II      Force non-interactive mode.  Default is to be interactive when
             run from a tty.

     --ii      Force interactive mode, even if not run from a tty.

     --mm      Causes ppkkgg__cchheecckk to always display the progress meter in cases it
             would not do so by default.

     --nn      Don't actually modify packages, just perform checks.

     --qq      Don't verify checksums for files, just check for their existence.
             Doubling --qq will bypass that check entirely.

     --vv      Turn on verbose output.  Several --vv may turn on more verbose out‐
             put.

     --xx      Disable progress meter.

